# 8. COMBAT AI

AI controls combat decision-making.

The AI evaluates:

```text
Current HP
Enemy HP
Distance
Threat
Allies
Enemy Position
Available Skills
Cooldown
Stamina
Mana
Emotional State
Morale
Fear
Personality
Orders
Battle Objective
Environment
Destruction Level
Permanent Death Risk
```

The AI then selects an action.

Because death is permanent, survival evaluation is a core part of Hero AI. A Hero may choose defense, retreat, protection, or support actions when the risk of death becomes too high.

---

# 9. AI DECISION MODEL

Basic structure:

```text
BATTLE STATE
      ↓
CHARACTER STATE
      ↓
LIFE STATE
      ↓
EMOTIONAL STATE
      ↓
PERSONALITY
      ↓
TACTICAL ANALYSIS
      ↓
MASTER ORDER
      ↓
AI DECISION
      ↓
ACTION
```

The Master can issue commands, but AI determines how the Hero executes the action.

A dead Hero has no AI decision and cannot perform any action.

---

# 10. MASTER COMMANDS

Basic commands:

```text
Attack
Defend
Focus Target
Protect
Use Skill
Use Item
Retreat
Hold Position
Support
Target Boss
Target Weak Enemy
```

These are tactical instructions rather than absolute animation commands.

The Master cannot command a permanently dead Hero.

---

# 11. COMMAND PRIORITY

Recommended decision priority:

```text
1. Permanent Survival
2. Critical Threat
3. Master Order
4. Party Protection
5. Objective
6. Tactical Advantage
7. Personal AI Preference
```

However, emotional conditions can modify these priorities.

A Hero may still take a lethal risk because of personality, emotional state, relationships, or story events. If the Hero dies as a result, the death is permanent.

