# 🌑 90. FINAL COMBAT PHILOSOPHY

The Basic Combat System is not designed to make Heroes behave like static units.

A Hero can:

```text
Become afraid.
Become angry.
Become determined.
Protect a friend.
Disobey an order.
Make a mistake.
Take a risk.
Remember their past.
Lose hope.
Find courage.
Die permanently.
```

The battlefield is also not static.

As the Master climbs the Tower:

```text
FLOOR
 ↓
DESTRUCTION
 ↓
ENVIRONMENT
 ↓
ENEMY
 ↓
HERO EMOTION
 ↓
AI BEHAVIOR
 ↓
BATTLE
 ↓
DEATH CHECK
 ↓
PERMANENT LOSS
 ↓
CONSEQUENCE
 ↓
GAME STATE
```

The result is that two battles against the same type of enemy do not necessarily have the same outcome.

A victory may still carry a permanent loss.

A retreat may save the remaining party.

A single tactical mistake may permanently remove a beloved Hero from the world.

